cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GAE-Δ in your research, please cite both the software and the article below."
title: "GAE-Δ: Phenotype-Specific Gene Role Shifts in Multi-Omics Data via Graph Autoencoder Embedding Differences"
abstract: >-
  GAE-Δ trains group-specific graph autoencoders on phenotype-stratified gene
  interaction networks and uses the difference between the learned gene
  embeddings to identify genes whose network role shifts between phenotypic
  groups, integrating RNA-seq, DNA methylation, and CNV via late fusion.
type: software
license: MIT
